[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPS-108
TITLE: Control Communication Interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware communicates with the main control board via one of the microcontroller's serial UART
interfaces. The firmware both receives and transmits data on this UART port. Due to the nature of
UART having independent transmit and receive lines, the transmit and receive functionality operate
independently. As the UART baud rate is relatively slow compared to the processing speed of the
microcontroller, both sending and receiving data is performed with nonblocking interrupt callback
functions.

Transmitted data is sent as a buffer of bytes, representing a singular data packet to the PC, with
the interrupt callback occurring once all data bytes have been transmitted. The firmware sets a flag
when transmission is initiated, and clears the flag after transmission is finished, to not create
transmission conflicts on the transmit line.

Reception is performed one byte at a time, with the interrupt callback occurring once a data byte is
available. The parsing of the received byte is done to determine whether a complete data packet has
been received from the PC, as according to the communication protocol. Once a completed data packet
has been received, the firmware sets a flag for further data processing outside of the parsing
inside of the interrupt callback.

As transmission on UART is asynchronous both in terms of clock as well as word alignment (within a
packet), a 'sync value' is utilized at the start of each packet to help synchronize communication in
case of any lost or missing bytes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-4
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPS-109
TITLE: Control Communication Data
STATEMENT: >>>
The data received from the main control board are commands to set various output control parameters
including grid voltage, filament current, high voltage, and output power. There are also commands to
initiate the process to test the high voltage and grid interlocks that the main control board
provides to the firmware.

The transmitted data to the main control board are the target setpoint values for, as well as the
monitored feedback values from, the HVPS. Additionally, status flags and IO values are reported by
the firmware.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-2
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
