[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPS-36
TITLE: Input Signals
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware logs several digital input signals coming from the HVPS and monitors the master fault
signal for determining if an HVPS fault has occurred.

The firmware also monitors three digital inputs from the main control board for enabling and
disabling emission: HV interlock, grid interlock, and the emission start signal.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-14
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPS-37
TITLE: Output Signals
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware controls various digital output signals. There are grid clocks and watchdog reset
signals which are toggled periodically by the firmware. Additionally, there are three digital
control signals which disable output on the HVPS: grid allowed, PFC allowed, and HV allowed. These
three signals correspond to three signals on the HVPS which similarly are used to disallow grid
switching, PFC enabling, and HV enabling on the HVPS. All these signals need to be appropriately
asserted for emission output to be enabled.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-14
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPS-123
TITLE: Logging Module
STATEMENT: >>>
The logging subsystem provides a configurable mechanism for recording and transmitting diagnostic information. It supports multiple log levels, formatted messages, and status reporting while minimizing application impact through buffered, asynchronous communication. The subsystem interfaces with the platform communication driver and provides a simple API for debugging, monitoring, and diagnostics.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-18
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWHVPS-124
TITLE: GET and SET Configurations Command Processing
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware processes GET and SET commands received through the FTDI UART interface to read and update configuration parameters. Valid requests are decoded, verified, and executed using the system configuration manager. GET commands return the requested parameter value, while successful SET commands update the parameter and return a confirmation response. Invalid requests are ignored without response.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWHVPS-18
  ROLE: Refines

